  "description": "Trap (audit finding: presumptive income declared below the deemed income could not be represented). s.44AD grocery trader: turnover 90,00,000 (cash 10,00,000 = 11.1% > 5%, so the Rs 2 crore limit applies; within it -> eligible). Deemed income 6% x 80,00,000 banking-channel = 4,80,000 + 8% x 10,00,000 = 80,000 -> 5,60,000. The trader declares 4,50,000 (its books profit), below the deemed income: the declared 4,50,000 is used (the old code took max(5,60,000, 4,50,000) = 5,60,000). New regime TI 4,50,000: 5% x 50,000 = 2,500, rebated u/s 87A (TI <= 12 lakh) -> nil. Old (comparison; old regime not available - no Form 10-IEA): 5% x 2,00,000 = 10,000, rebated u/s 87A (TI <= 5 lakh) -> nil. Declared below the deemed income, so the profit is not declared under s.44AD(1): TI 4,50,000 exceeds the basic exemption 4,00,000 -> tax audit u/s 44AB(e) read with s.44AD(4)-(5) (s.44AD(4) taken to apply; partner to confirm from the prior returns) -> block tax.audit-44ab (job planned as non-audit) and warn tax.presumptive-declared-lower; due date becomes 31-10-2026 (audit), planned filing 31-07-2026 is in time; ITR-3, not the ITR-4 planned -> warn tax.itr-form. No tax, no TDS, no advance-tax interest; nothing payable. presumptiveIncomePaise keeps the deemed 5,60,000; businessIncomePaise is the declared 4,50,000.",
